1
00:00:20,350 --> 00:00:24,447
Musaylimah(مسيلمة) was firm and he was in the heart of his army

2
00:00:24,740 --> 00:00:28,387
and his people were surrounding him from each direction,

3
00:00:28,427 --> 00:00:35,111
it was like a hurricane with Musaylimah(مسيلمة) in the middle, and they're just revolving around him and fighting.

4
00:00:35,529 --> 00:00:40,726
 Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) realized that there is no chance, we can stop these people from dying.

5
00:00:40,772 --> 00:00:44,150
 Because they were just dropping down dead; Banu Hanifa(بنوحنيفة), and the fight still going on.

6
00:00:44,370 --> 00:00:48,229
He realized that the only way is to get through to Musailimah Al-Kazzab(مسيلمة ألكذاب)

7
00:00:48,253 --> 00:00:51,098
Musaylimah(مسيلمة) was the heart of his army.

8
00:00:51,122 --> 00:00:53,245
 I mean, when At-Tabari(ألطبري) describes it, he says,

9
00:00:53,872 --> 00:00:59,648
Musaylimah(مسيلمة) stood firm, he was the eye of the storm, their mill revolved around him,

10
00:01:00,155 --> 00:01:03,874
it was like a mill revolving and he was the center, he was the eye of the storm.

11
00:01:04,573 --> 00:01:09,347
So Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) he took with him a group of Fursaan(فُرسان), knights.

12
00:01:09,711 --> 00:01:13,363
And he said: Let's just charge straightforward; break through their ranks

13
00:01:13,387 --> 00:01:15,503
until we get to Musaylimah(مسيلمة) himself and kill him.

14
00:01:16,054 --> 00:01:19,955
Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) even though, he's the Ameer(أمير) of the Army, he's the head of the army.

15
00:01:21,130 --> 00:01:27,822
He would just strike straight through the ranks of the enemy, cut it like a knife, cutting a loaf of bread.

16
00:01:28,269 --> 00:01:31,321
So Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) and his Fursaan(فُرسان) on top of their horses

17
00:01:31,832 --> 00:01:37,586
just broke through the ranks of the enemy, until they could see Musaylimah(مسيلمة) in front of their eyes.

18
00:01:38,438 --> 00:01:42,018
When that happened, Musaylimah(مسيلمة) and his army retreated.

19
00:01:43,634 --> 00:01:47,270
 And the Muslims just followed them killing them left and right in their retreat

20
00:01:47,665 --> 00:01:52,724
until they cornered them into a garden, a farm or ranch that was fortified.

21
00:01:53,201 --> 00:01:58,395
So Musaylimah(مسيلمة) and his people got into this ranch, they locked the gates.

22
00:01:58,672 --> 00:02:03,188
So now the Muslims were locked outside and unable to get in.

23
00:02:04,249 --> 00:02:07,034
Al-Bara'a Bin Malik(ألبرآءبن مالك) the brother of Anas Ibn Malik(أنس إبن مالك), he said:

24
00:02:07,058 --> 00:02:09,563
Throw me in, just throw me in.

25
00:02:10,700 --> 00:02:18,237
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب), he ordered Al-Bara'a(ألبراء) to join an army.

26
00:02:18,757 --> 00:02:21,704
But he sent with him a letter to the Ameer(أمير) of the army saying,

27
00:02:22,084 --> 00:02:25,793
Do not appoint Al-Bara'a(ألبراء) over any position of leadership

28
00:02:26,086 --> 00:02:29,350
because he will perish everyone with him.

29
00:02:30,659 --> 00:02:32,223
Anybody with Al-Bara'a(ألبراء) would just die.

30
00:02:32,555 --> 00:02:35,338
Don't give him any position of leadership, Let him do what he wants on his own

31
00:02:35,671 --> 00:02:37,917
but don't appoint him as a leader.

32
00:02:38,238 --> 00:02:39,964
Al-Bara'a(ألبراء) said just throw me on top of them.

33
00:02:41,154 --> 00:02:42,298
So they said: We're not going to do that.

34
00:02:42,338 --> 00:02:43,913
He said: I tell you, throw me.

35
00:02:44,447 --> 00:02:48,029
So, they put him on top of shield, they just picked him up.

36
00:02:48,494 --> 00:02:50,029
In one narration, they just threw him.

37
00:02:50,299 --> 00:02:52,252
In another narration, it says that they picked him up

38
00:02:52,575 --> 00:02:57,346
and when he saw the army of Musaylimah(مسيلمة) right under him

39
00:02:58,040 --> 00:02:59,846
he hesitated and he pulled back,

40
00:03:00,052 --> 00:03:03,958
he just saw a flood of people with the swords pointing up

41
00:03:04,859 --> 00:03:06,820
and then he took a breath and he said throw me.

42
00:03:07,211 --> 00:03:12,398
So they threw him in and the people of Musaylimah(مسيلمة), see this man falling down on them like a bird from the sky.

43
00:03:12,722 --> 00:03:16,253
He succeeded in fighting them away until, he gets to the gate.

44
00:03:16,671 --> 00:03:21,056
He opens the gate, picks up the keys and allows the Muslim army to come in

45
00:03:21,990 --> 00:03:24,578
and he had 80 injuries in his body or something like that.

46
00:03:26,386 --> 00:03:31,015
 The Muslims came in and now there's nowhere to go.

47
00:03:31,347 --> 00:03:36,662
The army of Musaylimah(مسيلمة) and the army of Khalid(خالد) are within this locked ranch.

48
00:03:37,373 --> 00:03:39,167
There is nothing to do but fight to death

49
00:03:40,796 --> 00:03:42,866
and now Musaylimah(مسيلمة) his Jin(جن) was coming to him.

50
00:03:42,890 --> 00:03:47,497
 They say: When his Jin(جن) would come to him, the foam would come out of his mouth

51
00:03:48,407 --> 00:03:50,533
and he would be obsessed with that Jin(جن),

52
00:03:51,072 --> 00:03:56,958
he had to throw himself to a wall and his eyes were just roaming around.

53
00:03:58,533 --> 00:04:02,264
At that moment Wahshee(وحشي) the killer of Hamza(حمزه)

54
00:04:03,980 --> 00:04:07,007
Wahshee(وحشي), the one who killed Hamza(حمزه), but later on became Muslim.

55
00:04:08,534 --> 00:04:14,426
He said: Just as I have killed the most beloved servant of Allah

56
00:04:15,430 --> 00:04:18,511
I'm going to compensate for that by killing the enemy of Allah.

57
00:04:19,444 --> 00:04:25,675
So he made it his target, that he's gonna use his skill to kill Musailimah Al-Kazzab(مسيلمة ألكذاب).

58
00:04:27,304 --> 00:04:31,836
 And he was very skilled in the Lances, throwing the spear.

59
00:04:32,871 --> 00:04:39,793
So he got him in his sights and he was able to strike Musailimah Al-Kazzab(مسيلمة ألكذاب)

60
00:04:39,818 --> 00:04:43,482
but at the same time Abu Dujana Al-Ansaari(أبودجانه ألأنصاري)

61
00:04:43,777 --> 00:04:48,924
the one who had the red band on his head in the Battle of Badr(بدر), took a hit at Musaylimah(مسيلمة).

62
00:04:49,309 --> 00:04:55,716
So it wasn't clear, who killed him and Wahshee(وحشي) would later on say, Our Lord knows who really killed him.

63
00:04:56,244 --> 00:04:58,396
But both of them took a strike at Musaylimah(مسيلمة)

64
00:04:58,697 --> 00:05:00,207
and because of that Musaylimah(مسيلمة) was dead,

65
00:05:00,319 --> 00:05:03,795
it was the spear of Wahshee(وحشي) and the sword of Abu Dujana(أبودجانة).

66
00:05:04,799 --> 00:05:09,481
With the death of Musaylimah(مسيلمة), the entire thing was over, that was the was the end.

67
00:05:10,600 --> 00:05:15,578
Musaylimah(مسيلمة) was the center in which the mill was revolving around.

68
00:05:16,113 --> 00:05:19,556
That garden was called Hadeeqa Tul Moat(حديقةالموت), the garden of death.

69
00:05:20,670 --> 00:05:23,426
The slogan of the Muslims on that day was

70
00:05:24,598 --> 00:05:26,855
Waa Muhammadah(وامحمداة), or Ya Muhammadah(يا محمداة).

71
00:05:27,489 --> 00:05:30,092
They were calling the name of Muhammadﷺ.

72
00:05:31,601 --> 00:05:34,954
Now, the calling of the name was symbolic, it was a slogan

73
00:05:34,978 --> 00:05:37,345
 it didn't mean that they were asking him for help

74
00:05:37,480 --> 00:05:40,234
because we know that that's something we're not allowed to do.

75
00:05:40,652 --> 00:05:43,171
But the Muslims had slogans in their wars.

76
00:05:44,575 --> 00:05:47,952
In one of these Saraya(سراية) Abu Salamah(أبوسلمة) says our slogan was

77
00:05:47,977 --> 00:05:50,224
Ammet(أمت), Ammet(أمت), kill, kill.

78
00:05:50,264 --> 00:05:53,412
In this battle, it was Ya Muhammadah(يا محمداة)

79
00:05:54,465 --> 00:05:56,282
that was their slogan in the battle.

80
00:05:58,167 --> 00:06:02,274
 There were ten thousand among the enemy killed, inside the garden.

81
00:06:03,589 --> 00:06:07,429
The number of Muslims, who were killed in the garden of death was 600.

82
00:06:09,458 --> 00:06:17,731
The total number of Muslims killed was 1200, so 600 in the garden and 600 outside.

83
00:06:18,096 --> 00:06:21,938
There are a few heroic acts that we need to talk about.

84
00:06:22,010 --> 00:06:28,100
Abu Aqeel(أبوعقيل) one of Al-Ansaar(أنْصَار), he was one of the first who were injured in the battle.

85
00:06:28,696 --> 00:06:33,078
He was struck by an arrow between his shoulder and his heart.

86
00:06:34,468 --> 00:06:40,153
It did not kill him, but it left his left side of the body weak.

87
00:06:41,857 --> 00:06:46,335
So he had to take rest in a tent, prepared for the injured.

88
00:06:48,575 --> 00:06:52,982
He heard Ma'an Bin Qais(معن بن قيس), make a call

89
00:06:53,337 --> 00:06:55,271
يا للأنصار الله الله

90
00:06:55,954 --> 00:06:58,352
O Ansaar(أنْصَار) Allah Allah, Allah Allah,

91
00:06:58,630 --> 00:07:00,175
ألقرَّة  على عداء الله

92
00:07:00,507 --> 00:07:01,779
Attack the enemies of Allah.

93
00:07:04,668 --> 00:07:08,023
Abu Aqeel(أبوعقيل), he tried to stand up and picked up his sword.

94
00:07:09,129 --> 00:07:11,394
So the Sahabah(صحابه) told him what are you doing?

95
00:07:12,877 --> 00:07:14,898
He said: Ma'an(معن) has called my name.

96
00:07:15,562 --> 00:07:18,061
They said: He didn't call your name, he's calling the Ansaar(أنْصَار).

97
00:07:18,653 --> 00:07:20,747
He said: I am one of Al-Ansaar(أنْصَار).

98
00:07:21,080 --> 00:07:23,505
They said: Well, you're injured there's no fighting for you.

99
00:07:23,876 --> 00:07:28,893
He said: I am one of Al-Ansaar(أنْصَار) and I heard my name was called

100
00:07:29,233 --> 00:07:32,277
and I am going to respond to the call even if I have to crawl.

101
00:07:34,306 --> 00:07:39,612
And he picked up his sword and he went to fight and he can't use his left hand to protect himself.

102
00:07:39,757 --> 00:07:43,967
So now he was fighting without protection and he was injured and he fell down.

103
00:07:44,763 --> 00:07:49,791
And towards his last moments before he died, Abdullah Ibn Umar رضي الله عنه approached him.

104
00:07:51,336 --> 00:07:57,687
So Abu Aqeel(أبوعقيل) said: Who does this day belong to? Who does this day belong to?

105
00:07:58,880 --> 00:07:59,940
Ibn Umar(إبن عُمَر) said;

106
00:08:00,423 --> 00:08:03,018
أبشِر فقد قتل عدوالله

107
00:08:03,111 --> 00:08:06,100
Rejoice because the enemy of Allah was killed.

108
00:08:06,890 --> 00:08:09,273
Abu Aqeel(أبوعقيل) said: Al-Hamdulillah(ألحمدلله) and then he passed away.

109
00:08:10,042 --> 00:08:12,987
 All what he wanted to know, who does that day belong to?

110
00:08:13,397 --> 00:08:16,353
 Does it belong to the Muslims, or does it belong to Musaylimah(مسيلمة)?

111
00:08:17,037 --> 00:08:22,088
And when he knew that the enemy of Allah was killed? He said: Al-Hamdulillah(ألحمدلله)!

112
00:08:22,639 --> 00:08:26,844
Nusaibah Bint Ka'ab(نصيبة بنت كعب), she made an oath that she's not going to lay down her sword

113
00:08:26,890 --> 00:08:34,131
 unless Musaylimah(مسيلمة) is killed and she participated in the fighting, the actual fighting.

114
00:08:35,314 --> 00:08:39,130
Nusaibah Bint Ka'ab(نصيبة بنت كعب) was left with 12 injuries.

115
00:08:40,105 --> 00:08:42,909
So she had to be tended to, in a tent

116
00:08:43,753 --> 00:08:48,827
and she said that Khalid Ibn Walid رضي الله عنه took so much care for me.

117
00:08:49,662 --> 00:08:59,595
He sent me a doctor, who would tend to my injuries and they use boiling oil to seal my injuries.

118
00:08:59,798 --> 00:09:05,300
She said: I would rather have my limbs amputated, then go through that pain.

119
00:09:07,399 --> 00:09:12,734
To seal the injury and to clean it from any infections.

120
00:09:12,974 --> 00:09:18,055
They would pour boiling oil to just burn the entire injury

121
00:09:18,080 --> 00:09:20,833
that was their medical treatment of the day.

122
00:09:21,548 --> 00:09:25,701
Obviously without any anesthesia without any painkillers - Allah O Akbar(الله أكبر)!

123
00:09:26,345 --> 00:09:35,202
Just think about a woman fighting and being injured and then she has to go through all of this pain.

124
00:09:36,338 --> 00:09:38,920
And now the Ummah(امة) men and women are laid back and relaxed

125
00:09:38,944 --> 00:09:45,657
and not realizing their duties towards Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ, not willing to suffer any pain, for the religion of Allah.

126
00:09:46,658 --> 00:09:49,720
The Sahabah رضي الله عنهم for them Islam was not lip service and talk.

127
00:09:50,539 --> 00:09:54,479
It was struggling, it was effort and it was some physical pain.

128
00:09:54,640 --> 00:09:56,686
 They went through a lot of physical pain.

129
00:09:57,403 --> 00:09:59,809
I mean, imagine what Nusaibah Bint Ka'ab(نصيبة بنت كعب) went through.

130
00:10:00,260 --> 00:10:05,183
 If one of your teeth will be plucked out without any painkiller.

131
00:10:06,470 --> 00:10:09,093
You would be thinking a lot before you go to the dentist.

132
00:10:10,022 --> 00:10:12,244
Now, Nusaibah Bint Ka'ab(نصيبة بنت كعب) took the decision to fight

133
00:10:12,289 --> 00:10:15,331
and she knew very well that there are some consequences of that.

134
00:10:15,759 --> 00:10:20,549
First of all, the injury itself is very painful and then to cure it, is very painful too

135
00:10:22,065 --> 00:10:24,525
but they took that decision consciously.

136
00:10:25,838 --> 00:10:28,978
Because they would rather do that for Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ then suffer on the Day of Judgment.

137
00:10:30,450 --> 00:10:32,237
نسعل الله عزوجل أن يقيم من عذاب

138
00:10:32,261 --> 00:10:35,110
We ask Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ to spare us from all punishment.

139
00:10:36,288 --> 00:10:38,966
And note here on the role that women used to play.

140
00:10:39,753 --> 00:10:42,265
Nusaibah Bint Ka'ab(نصيبة بنت كعب) participated in actual fighting

141
00:10:42,559 --> 00:10:45,179
tells you a lot about the role of early Muslim women.

142
00:10:45,755 --> 00:10:53,276
 Also Umm Tamim(أم تميم) the wife of Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) was given the responsibility of guarding a prisoner of war.

143
00:10:54,231 --> 00:11:02,339
So in addition to their supportive roles of nursing, and providing food, and supplements to the army

144
00:11:02,905 --> 00:11:05,504
there were also some combative roles

145
00:11:05,571 --> 00:11:08,190
like what Nusaibah Bint Ka'ab(نصيبة بنت كعب) was involved in

146
00:11:08,627 --> 00:11:11,887
and also the security guard role

147
00:11:12,524 --> 00:11:15,637
that Umm Tamim(أم تميم), the wife of Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) had.

148
00:11:17,758 --> 00:11:22,652
The Shuhadaa(شهداء) of the battle of Al-Yamamah(أليمامة)

149
00:11:23,716 --> 00:11:26,033
Thabit Bin Qais رضي الله عنه,

150
00:11:26,511 --> 00:11:29,265
one who held the banner of Al-Ansaar(أنْصَار).

151
00:11:30,863 --> 00:11:36,119
The one, who set his foot in the ground, so that he would not retreat, he was killed.

152
00:11:38,322 --> 00:11:41,408
One of the Muslim soldiers saw a dream after Thabit(ثابت) was killed.

153
00:11:41,966 --> 00:11:47,651
 This was mentioned by Ibn Kathir(اِبْنِ كَثِيْر), in this dream Thabit(ثابت) comes to him and tells him

154
00:11:48,671 --> 00:11:55,378
when I was killed a Muslim came to me and took away a very valuable shield that I have.

155
00:11:56,726 --> 00:12:02,862
And this Muslim is in such and such place, you'll find his horse next to it.

156
00:12:03,570 --> 00:12:08,317
And then you'll find my shield on top of it is a rock and on top of it, is a saddle.

157
00:12:09,736 --> 00:12:13,102
 Go and take my shield, give it to Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد)

158
00:12:13,653 --> 00:12:18,966
and tell him to send it to Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) and to have him sell it, to pay my debts

159
00:12:19,565 --> 00:12:21,846
that belongs to so and so.

160
00:12:22,361 --> 00:12:24,726
And then Thabit(ثابت) told this man in the dream.

161
00:12:25,272 --> 00:12:27,542
وإيَّاك أن تقول هذا حُلُم فتضيهَا

162
00:12:28,417 --> 00:12:32,373
And be aware to say that this is a dream, so I'm going to neglect it.

163
00:12:33,277 --> 00:12:34,511
He said: This is serious.

164
00:12:35,860 --> 00:12:41,818
So the man wakes up and he goes and just as I was described in the dream he finds the shield

165
00:12:41,858 --> 00:12:44,464
and he takes it to Khalid(خالد), Khalid(خالد) sends it to Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

166
00:12:44,496 --> 00:12:48,072
Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) sells it and they pay off the debt of Thabit(ثابت).

167
00:12:48,373 --> 00:12:51,214
So his will was given after his death.

168
00:12:51,719 --> 00:12:53,829
He gave his will after his death.

169
00:12:54,329 --> 00:12:55,960
It's a Karamah(كرامة) for Thabit Bin Qais(ثابت بن قيس)

170
00:12:56,026 --> 00:12:59,337
because you know that you are held captive and you cannot enter into Jannah(جنة)

171
00:12:59,488 --> 00:13:00,609
until you pay your debts.

172
00:13:02,598 --> 00:13:05,178
Zaid Ibn Khattab رضي الله عنه the brother Umar(عُمَر).

173
00:13:06,035 --> 00:13:09,043
When the news reached Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه, he said;

174
00:13:09,067 --> 00:13:15,348
رحم الله زيد، سبقني إلى الحُسنَيين، أسلم قبلي، واستُشهد قبلي

175
00:13:15,790 --> 00:13:23,039
May Allah have mercy on Zaid(زيد), he came first before me, in the two greatest things

176
00:13:23,063 --> 00:13:25,498
becoming a Muslim and becoming Shaheed(شَهِيد).

177
00:13:26,917 --> 00:13:30,561
He became a Muslim before me and he became a Shaheed(شَهِيد) before me.

178
00:13:31,198 --> 00:13:35,130
Obviously Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was happy that his brother died as a Shaheed(شَهِيد) but

179
00:13:36,228 --> 00:13:41,113
 because when Abdullah Ibn Umar رضي الله عنه came back from the Ghazwa(غزوة)

180
00:13:42,316 --> 00:13:45,118
as soon as he came in and met his father.

181
00:13:45,848 --> 00:13:47,750
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) told him;

182
00:13:48,277 --> 00:13:52,900
Abdullah(عبدالله)! How dare you show me your face?

183
00:13:53,966 --> 00:13:56,939
Why didn't you die as a Shaheed(شَهِيد) as your uncle died?

184
00:13:59,010 --> 00:14:01,505
This tells you a lot about the Tarbiyah(تربية) of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب)

185
00:14:02,206 --> 00:14:04,784
and the Tarbiyah(تربية) of the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم to their children.

186
00:14:05,085 --> 00:14:08,376
He didn't hug him and say, Al-hamdulillah(ألحمدلله) you came back safe.

187
00:14:09,123 --> 00:14:13,673
I wish that you didn't even go out, you disobeyed me, by going out to fight.

188
00:14:14,794 --> 00:14:17,270
He said: How dare you show me your face.?

189
00:14:17,776 --> 00:14:19,860
When your uncle died as a Shaheed(شَهِيد) and you didn't.

190
00:14:20,607 --> 00:14:23,045
Abdullah Ibn Umar(عبدالله ابن عمر) said: O Father, I asked for it.

191
00:14:23,737 --> 00:14:25,862
But Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ blessed my uncle with it.

192
00:14:26,686 --> 00:14:29,127
And Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ decided that I would live for another day.

193
00:14:32,296 --> 00:14:35,986
So Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه was happy that his brother has died as a Shaheed(شَهِيد).

194
00:14:36,537 --> 00:14:40,688
But still, it left a very significant scar on the heart of Umar(عُمَر)

195
00:14:41,575 --> 00:14:43,115
and he would always remember his brother.

196
00:14:44,072 --> 00:14:46,836
 In fact, whenever the wind would blow from the North.

197
00:14:47,009 --> 00:14:47,642
 Ar-Reeh-Us-Suba(ألريح صبح)

198
00:14:48,341 --> 00:14:50,532
because the battle happened in Al-Yamamah(أليمامة), which is North.

199
00:14:51,239 --> 00:14:54,875
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: Whenever the wind would blow from the north,

200
00:14:54,899 --> 00:14:56,684
it would remind me my brother Zaid(زيد).

201
00:14:58,478 --> 00:15:02,443
Mutammum Bin Nuwairah(متمم بن نويرة), the brother of Malik(مالك), who was killed by Khalid(خالد).

202
00:15:03,674 --> 00:15:06,545
He made some lines of poetry talking about his brother.

203
00:15:07,861 --> 00:15:12,068
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) when he heard those lines. He said;

204
00:15:12,931 --> 00:15:18,479
I wish that I had that ability to say poetry if I did, I would say similar words.

205
00:15:19,556 --> 00:15:21,227
In the obituary of my brother.

206
00:15:21,869 --> 00:15:24,735
Mutammam(متمم) told Umar(عُمَر), he said;

207
00:15:25,247 --> 00:15:29,639
لو أنَّ أخي ذهب على ما ذهب عليه أخوك ما حزنة عليه

208
00:15:30,338 --> 00:15:35,026
 If my brother died the same way for the same cause your brother died.

209
00:15:35,469 --> 00:15:41,984
I wouldn't have had any sadness for him, I wouldn't have regretted his death.

210
00:15:43,107 --> 00:15:45,107
Your brother died as a Shaheed(شَهِيد).

211
00:15:45,639 --> 00:15:50,042
If my brother Malik(مالك) died in the same situation for the same cause that your brother died,

212
00:15:50,258 --> 00:15:52,165
 I wouldn't have had any regret.

213
00:15:52,643 --> 00:15:53,706
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said;

214
00:15:54,037 --> 00:15:56,536
ما عزاني أحد بمثل ما أذيتنى به

215
00:15:56,787 --> 00:16:01,619
No one has ever given me counsel like you did.

216
00:16:02,587 --> 00:16:05,249
Nobody has given me condolences, like you did.

217
00:16:05,551 --> 00:16:07,130
This is the best thing I've ever heard.

218
00:16:08,436 --> 00:16:10,450
 The fact that my brother dies is a Shaheed(شَهِيد).

219
00:16:11,356 --> 00:16:14,521
 I shouldn't have any sadness or sorrow because of that.

220
00:16:15,415 --> 00:16:17,536
The brother of Zaid(زيد)

221
00:16:17,784 --> 00:16:21,930
the brotherhood that was made between Muhajireen(مهاجرين) Wal Ansaar(ولأنْصَار) in Madina

222
00:16:22,555 --> 00:16:23,795
was Ma'an Bin Udae(معان بن عدي),

223
00:16:24,668 --> 00:16:29,346
Rasool Ullah appointed Zaid Ibn Khattab(زيد إبن خطاب) to be the brother of Ma'an Bin Udae(معان بن عدي).

224
00:16:30,053 --> 00:16:34,135
Now, we know that that brotherhood of Al-Akhuwa(ألأخوة)

225
00:16:34,167 --> 00:16:40,267
that was instituted as soon as Al-Muhajiroon(ألمهاجرون) went into Madina was later abrogated.

226
00:16:42,030 --> 00:16:46,144
 Because it was a brotherhood that was put ahead of Brotherhood of Blood.

227
00:16:46,309 --> 00:16:51,212
So even in terms of inheritance, they would inherit each other, that was abrogated.

228
00:16:51,560 --> 00:16:55,893
However, the relationship between many of these brothers continued on, to be a special relationship

229
00:16:56,059 --> 00:16:58,456
and this was the case between Zaid(زيد) and Ma'an(معان).

230
00:16:59,679 --> 00:17:04,037
They continue to having that very close friendship, until the last day.

231
00:17:04,340 --> 00:17:08,292
So Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ, His Qadar(قَدَر) was that they die the same day.

232
00:17:09,272 --> 00:17:12,394
So Ma'an Bin Udae(معان بن عدي) died in that battle.

233
00:17:13,361 --> 00:17:17,376
Ma'an Bin Udae(معان بن عدي), he had a very amazing statement when Rasool Allah ﷺ died.

234
00:17:17,661 --> 00:17:24,263
Some of the Sahabah(صحابه) said: We wish that we have died before Rasool Allah ﷺ died.

235
00:17:25,019 --> 00:17:27,547
 Ma'an Bin Udae(معان بن عدي) said: I would not desire that

236
00:17:28,051 --> 00:17:32,360
because I want to believe in Muhammadﷺ dead as I believed him alive.

237
00:17:33,263 --> 00:17:38,429
I wanted to believe in Muhammadﷺ when he is dead, just as I believed in him when he was alive.

238
00:17:40,050 --> 00:17:43,596
Abdullah Bin Suhail Bin Amr(عبدالله بن سهيل بن عمرو) also was a Shaheed(شَهِيد).

239
00:17:44,467 --> 00:17:51,117
Sohail Ibn Amr(سهيل إبن عمرو) was the one, who signed the contract with Rasool Allah ﷺ in Hudaybiyah(حديبية).

240
00:17:51,804 --> 00:17:53,802
 His son Abdullah(عبدالله) was one of the Muslims

241
00:17:53,889 --> 00:17:58,139
 who were handed over to the Mushrikeen(مشركين) according to the terms of the agreement, Abdullah(عبدالله).

242
00:17:58,668 --> 00:18:01,142
The terms of the agreement of Al-Hudaybiyah(ألحديبية) stated that

243
00:18:01,616 --> 00:18:04,641
if a Muslim comes from Makkah to Madina, he should be returned.

244
00:18:04,903 --> 00:18:09,337
But if an apostate goes from Madina to Makkah they are not returned.

245
00:18:10,458 --> 00:18:12,974
Abdullah(عبدالله) was a Muslim who came from Makkah to Madina

246
00:18:12,998 --> 00:18:15,276
and according to the terms of the agreement, he had to be returned.

247
00:18:15,679 --> 00:18:19,034
So he stayed in Makkah and was persecuted.

248
00:18:20,304 --> 00:18:23,345
He came out with the Mushrikeen(مشركين) in the Battle of Badr(بدر).

249
00:18:23,893 --> 00:18:28,060
He came alongside the army and as soon as they reached the battleground,

250
00:18:28,084 --> 00:18:30,017
he ran away and joined the Muslims.

251
00:18:31,326 --> 00:18:34,049
He died as a Shaheed(شَهِيد) in this battle.

252
00:18:35,595 --> 00:18:39,352
Abu Dujana(أبودجانة), the one with the red band on the Badr(بدر),

253
00:18:39,439 --> 00:18:41,817
 who was marching in front of the army with pride.

254
00:18:43,299 --> 00:18:45,591
So as a Muslim you're not supposed to be arrogant.

255
00:18:45,878 --> 00:18:48,663
 And that was a very arrogant way of walking.

256
00:18:49,644 --> 00:18:52,722
So some of the Muslims were wondering. Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

257
00:18:53,382 --> 00:18:58,235
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ dislikes this way of walking except in this situation

258
00:18:59,124 --> 00:19:02,085
because he's doing it to terrify the enemy of Allah.

259
00:19:02,402 --> 00:19:07,421
 Abu Dujana(أبودجانة) was the partner of Wahshee(وحشي) in killing Musaylimah(مسيلمة)

260
00:19:07,824 --> 00:19:10,331
He also died in this battle.

261
00:19:11,411 --> 00:19:16,592
At-Tufail Bin Amr Ad-Dausi(ألطفيل بن عمرو ألدؤسي) was the chief of his people Daus(دؤس).

262
00:19:17,957 --> 00:19:22,318
He was with his son Amr(عمرو) and he told him: O son, I saw a dream.

263
00:19:24,495 --> 00:19:29,899
 I saw that my head was shaven, and a bird came out from my mouth.

264
00:19:31,552 --> 00:19:34,785
And a womb of a woman swallowed me.

265
00:19:36,062 --> 00:19:41,309
he said: My son, I interpret that to mean Shahadah(شَهَادَة).

266
00:19:41,735 --> 00:19:47,710
The shaving of my head is my killing, and the bird coming out from my mouth is my soul.

267
00:19:48,636 --> 00:19:54,115
And the woman swallowing me in her womb, is the earth, I will be buried

268
00:19:55,889 --> 00:20:00,354
and his dream was fulfilled in the Battle of Yamamah(يمامة).

269
00:20:01,399 --> 00:20:06,210
Abbad Bin Bishr(عبَّادبن بشر) one of the notables among Al-Ansaar رضي الله عنهم

270
00:20:06,761 --> 00:20:11,907
he was part of the Special Operations team that assassinated Ka'ab Ibn Al-Ashraf(كعب إبن ألأشرف).

271
00:20:13,700 --> 00:20:18,495
One night Rasool Allah ﷺ was praying Tahajjud(تهجد) late at night

272
00:20:20,932 --> 00:20:24,224
and the room of Ayesha(عائشه) was adjacent to the Masjid(مسجد).

273
00:20:24,963 --> 00:20:29,336
 So Rasool Allah ﷺ was hearing the recitation of Qur'an come from Al-Masjid(مسجد).

274
00:20:30,326 --> 00:20:35,509
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ said: O Ayesha(عائشه) is this the voice of Abbad(عَبَّاد)?

275
00:20:36,607 --> 00:20:41,402
Ayesha(عائشه) said: Yes! Rasool Allah ﷺ said: May Allah have mercy on him

276
00:20:42,765 --> 00:20:43,611
and this is in Bukhari(بخاريْ).

277
00:20:45,428 --> 00:20:49,851
 And usually when Rasool Allah ﷺ would make a Dua(دُعَا), for Allah to have mercy on someone

278
00:20:50,201 --> 00:20:52,896
what would happen to that person? He dies as a Shaheed(شَهِيد)

279
00:20:54,258 --> 00:20:55,789
as if mercy of Allah is Shahadah(شَهَادَة).

280
00:20:58,098 --> 00:21:03,360
Because once there was one of the Ansaar(أنْصَار), who was making Anasheed(أناشيد) for the army.

281
00:21:04,920 --> 00:21:10,116
 So, Rasool Allah ﷺ said: May Allah have mercy on him

282
00:21:10,228 --> 00:21:11,756
 Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: O Rasool Ullah

283
00:21:11,791 --> 00:21:12,828
لَو لَا متعتنا به

284
00:21:12,866 --> 00:21:13,725
O Rasool Ullah

285
00:21:14,835 --> 00:21:15,898
لَو لَا متعتنا به

286
00:21:15,922 --> 00:21:19,471
We wanted to enjoy him, meaning you have taken away his life now.

287
00:21:19,879 --> 00:21:20,953
We wanted to enjoy him.

288
00:21:21,422 --> 00:21:25,987
So the Dua(دُعَا) of Rahma(رحمة) by Rasool Allah ﷺ means that the person will die as a Shaheed(شَهِيد).

289
00:21:28,082 --> 00:21:32,790
 He also saw dreams. So Karamaat(كرامات) and dreams happen a lot to the Mujahideen(مجاهدين)

290
00:21:33,723 --> 00:21:34,476
because of the Sidq(صدق)

291
00:21:35,231 --> 00:21:37,451
أصدقكم حديثًا أصدقكم رُؤيَّا

292
00:21:37,476 --> 00:21:43,541
The most truthful of you in words are the most true in their dreams.

293
00:21:43,717 --> 00:21:45,770
 Their dreams are not deceptive, their dreams are true.

294
00:21:46,790 --> 00:21:54,651
And a person who is in the path of Allah fighting in the sake of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ represents truth

295
00:21:55,466 --> 00:21:59,521
 because you are giving up your life for Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

296
00:22:00,030 --> 00:22:04,911
So he saw a dream that, he told one of his companions, he said;

297
00:22:05,306 --> 00:22:11,049
I saw a dream that the sky opened, the heavens opened and I went through and then it closed

298
00:22:11,853 --> 00:22:14,596
and I interpret that to mean Shahadah(شَهَادَة).

299
00:22:16,110 --> 00:22:19,766
 He saw that after the Battle of buzakha(بزاخة), which we talked about with Tulaiha(طليحة)

300
00:22:20,579 --> 00:22:21,889
and the dream was fulfilled.

301
00:22:22,161 --> 00:22:25,117
 During the battle Abbad Bin Bishr(عبَّادبن بشر),

302
00:22:25,883 --> 00:22:31,037
he went on top of a hill and called Al-Ansaar(أنْصَار), so now you mobilize your own people.

303
00:22:32,281 --> 00:22:37,797
The Ansaar(أنْصَار), they give motivation to the Ansaar(أنْصَار), and Muhajiroon(مهاجرون) because it's competition

304
00:22:38,253 --> 00:22:43,787
nobody wants to be the one, who will be the cause of the defeat of the Muslims

305
00:22:43,811 --> 00:22:46,886
and every tribe that would call on their own people.

306
00:22:46,906 --> 00:22:50,205
So now Abbad Bin Bishr(عبَّادبن بشر) is trying to motivate Al-Ansaar(اَلْاَنْصَار)

307
00:22:50,229 --> 00:22:53,178
he stood up on a hill, so they could all see him and he called them.

308
00:22:53,363 --> 00:22:56,530
So, a big group of them came to him and what he did is,

309
00:22:56,578 --> 00:23:00,606
he took the Sheath of his sword and he broke it on his knees.

310
00:23:00,915 --> 00:23:05,301
So, when the Ansaar(أنْصَار) saw that they broke theirs and that means this sword is not going back.

311
00:23:06,646 --> 00:23:12,425
And he said: Go ahead with truth, and they attacked

312
00:23:12,854 --> 00:23:19,267
and many of them were killed in that attack, he was killed at the age of 45.

313
00:23:20,230 --> 00:23:30,290
Abbad Bin Bishr(عبَّادبن بشر) with his group played a very important role, in pushing the people of Musaylimah(مسيلمة) into the farm.

314
00:23:30,830 --> 00:23:34,952
And then they went in and fought with them, in closed gates.

315
00:23:35,652 --> 00:23:39,441
Abbad Bin Bishr(عبَّادبن بشر) did so much that day in fighting

316
00:23:39,750 --> 00:23:42,715
 that he became an example later on among Banu Hanifa(بنوحنيفة).

317
00:23:43,156 --> 00:23:44,804
Whenever they would see somebody injured

318
00:23:45,152 --> 00:23:50,196
they would say you're injured by the Mujarrib(مُجَرِّب) the experienced man, Abbad Bin Bishr(عبَّادبن بشر).

319
00:23:50,803 --> 00:23:54,845
His fighting on that day became an example for the people,

320
00:23:55,861 --> 00:23:57,907
 رضي الله عنه وَاَرضاہ

321
00:23:59,574 --> 00:24:01,148
So the battle was over.

322
00:24:01,965 --> 00:24:08,069
Now Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) wants to see this man, who was root of the whole problem, Musaylimah(مسيلمة).

323
00:24:08,475 --> 00:24:10,007
So he took with him with Muja'ah(مجاعة),

324
00:24:10,028 --> 00:24:10,999
who was Muja'ah(مجاعة)?

325
00:24:11,595 --> 00:24:13,293
His captive, the hostage.

326
00:24:13,516 --> 00:24:15,109
Who's in the tent of his wife.

327
00:24:15,747 --> 00:24:20,072
So now he's holding Muja'ah(مجاعة), and they're strolling through the dead bodies.

328
00:24:21,328 --> 00:24:24,847
And Khalid(خالد) wants to know, who's Musaylimah(مسيلمة)

329
00:24:25,261 --> 00:24:29,496
so they pass next to Ar-Rajjal(ألرجال) and he says, this is Ar-Rajjal Bin Unfua(ألرجال بن عنفوة).

330
00:24:30,725 --> 00:24:34,166
And then they go on and they enter into the garden of death.

331
00:24:35,670 --> 00:24:38,727
And then Muja'ah(مجاعة) points to Musailimah Al-Kazzab(مسيلمة ألكذاب)

332
00:24:39,561 --> 00:24:44,230
when Khalid(خالد) takes a look at this man, he said: This is the one,

333
00:24:44,769 --> 00:24:46,338
ألَّذي فعل بكم لأفاعيل

334
00:24:46,364 --> 00:24:48,198
This is the one, who did to you what he did.?

335
00:24:49,930 --> 00:24:56,643
The way he looks, doesn't reflect what evil and influence, he has caused.

336
00:24:57,676 --> 00:24:59,530
So Muja'ah(مجاعة) said: Yes, this is the one.

337
00:25:01,483 --> 00:25:09,378
Muja'ah(مجاعة) told Khalid(خالد) that I want to strike a deal with you, for my people,

338
00:25:09,515 --> 00:25:13,892
Banu Hanifa(بنوحنيفة) were different clans a conglomeration of Clans.

339
00:25:14,790 --> 00:25:16,869
So Muja'ah(مجاعة) tells Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد)

340
00:25:17,084 --> 00:25:19,361
 I want to make a truce with you for my people.

341
00:25:19,940 --> 00:25:23,589
I pay you this amount of gold, silver and armory.

342
00:25:24,711 --> 00:25:27,340
Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) could continue fighting

343
00:25:28,455 --> 00:25:32,968
 because he sent his army to just pick up the many of the other fortresses.

344
00:25:33,271 --> 00:25:36,000
Take all of the women and children and wealth, all of it.

345
00:25:36,560 --> 00:25:44,414
 But Muja'ah(مجاعة) he told Khalid(خالد) there are many fighters in my fortress.

346
00:25:45,217 --> 00:25:48,492
So let me strike a deal with you, this is what I will pay you.

347
00:25:49,605 --> 00:25:53,340
Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) said: Alright, go and discuss with your people, so he goes

348
00:25:54,057 --> 00:25:56,337
Muja'ah(مجاعة) goes into his fortress, there are no men,

349
00:25:56,732 --> 00:26:00,464
except the elderly and the weak, women and children.

350
00:26:00,906 --> 00:26:04,614
 He told them all to dress up in armory

351
00:26:05,134 --> 00:26:08,724
and he told the women to take out their hair on their chest

352
00:26:08,748 --> 00:26:11,056
because men in those days used to grow their hair long.

353
00:26:11,677 --> 00:26:18,098
So he told the women to hang their hair and to wear turbans and helmets and armory

354
00:26:18,123 --> 00:26:27,188
and carry weapons and to stand on top of the roofs and on the guarding points of this fort.

355
00:26:28,458 --> 00:26:29,918
And Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد), he is in a distance.

356
00:26:29,958 --> 00:26:31,995
So, the Muslims cannot see the faces.

357
00:26:32,611 --> 00:26:35,311
So Muja'ah(مجاعة) comes back and tells Khalid(خالد) my people refused.

358
00:26:36,839 --> 00:26:40,079
But let me try another deal with them, so he reduced the amount and said;

359
00:26:40,103 --> 00:26:41,364
I'll go and try with my people.

360
00:26:43,282 --> 00:26:45,223
And they're ready to fight you and take a look.

361
00:26:45,612 --> 00:26:47,080
Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) takes a look.

362
00:26:47,360 --> 00:26:52,477
 A blanket of black, is all what he sees covering the roofs.

363
00:26:54,387 --> 00:26:59,454
Now Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) was exhausted from fighting and his army were weak.

364
00:27:00,592 --> 00:27:08,140
Because the Battle of Al-Yamamah(أليمامة) was the most vicious battle that the Muslims have been in so far.

365
00:27:09,108 --> 00:27:11,188
1200 Muslims were killed.

366
00:27:11,345 --> 00:27:16,234
That was the biggest single day loss ever, for the muslims.

367
00:27:16,600 --> 00:27:19,034
About 300 of Al-Muhajireen(مهاجرين) Wal-Ansaar(واَلْاَنْصَار)

368
00:27:19,592 --> 00:27:23,186
 about 60 or 50 from Haffaz Al-Qur'an(حفاظ ألقرآن) were killed on that day.

369
00:27:23,971 --> 00:27:26,629
So even though the news of victory reached to Madina

370
00:27:27,375 --> 00:27:31,182
 but the news of the dead, subdued the tone of happiness

371
00:27:31,533 --> 00:27:35,109
because it was the greatest loss that the Muslims have ever suffered so far.

372
00:27:36,341 --> 00:27:41,883
 Now the losses among Banu Hanifa(بنوحنيفة) were greater, I mean, 10,000 were killed in the garden of death,

373
00:27:42,304 --> 00:27:44,093
 let alone the ones were killed outside.

374
00:27:44,629 --> 00:27:48,494
So the Muslims are exhausted, tired, and they needed rest.

375
00:27:48,952 --> 00:27:53,081
So now Khalid(خالد) takes a look at this blanket of people covering the roofs.

376
00:27:53,343 --> 00:27:56,038
He said: Fine, I agree.

377
00:27:57,046 --> 00:27:58,712
Muja'ah(مجاعة) said: Let's write it down.

378
00:27:59,098 --> 00:28:02,014
 They write it down and he opens the gates.

379
00:28:02,604 --> 00:28:05,299
The Muslims go in, there's nobody but children and women.

380
00:28:06,717 --> 00:28:08,121
Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) said: You tricked me.

381
00:28:08,977 --> 00:28:12,194
 Muja'ah(مجاعة) said: I did what I have to do to save my people.

382
00:28:13,815 --> 00:28:14,895
These are my kinship.

383
00:28:15,482 --> 00:28:16,801
I did, what I have to do.

384
00:28:17,612 --> 00:28:20,605
Khalid(خالد) told Muja'ah(مجاعة) marry me, your daughter.

385
00:28:21,686 --> 00:28:25,902
Muja'ah(مجاعة) said: That will ruin my reputation and ruin yours, with your leader.

386
00:28:26,250 --> 00:28:29,867
Khalid(خالد) Said: Man! I'm telling you to marry me, your daughter.

387
00:28:31,909 --> 00:28:35,005
 He said: Fine, I marry you, my daughter.

388
00:28:35,853 --> 00:28:38,125
The news reaches to Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه

389
00:28:38,620 --> 00:28:41,343
that Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) has married again.

390
00:28:42,034 --> 00:28:44,002
He sends a letter. He says;

391
00:28:44,547 --> 00:28:53,820
يابن أم خالد إنك لفارغ تنكح النساء وبفناء بيتك دم ألف ومائتي رجل من المسلمين

392
00:28:54,105 --> 00:29:00,372
لم يجفف بعد ثم خذعك مجاعة راعيك فصالحك عن قومه وقد أمكن الله منهم

393
00:29:01,306 --> 00:29:03,235
O son of the mother of Khalid(خالد)!

394
00:29:04,454 --> 00:29:07,150
You find yourself free to marry women.

395
00:29:07,811 --> 00:29:14,814
When in your court yard is the blood of 1200 Muslims and their blood did not dry yet.

396
00:29:15,978 --> 00:29:21,952
And then you allow Maja'ah(مجاعة) to trick you, when Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ has handed them over to you.

397
00:29:22,729 --> 00:29:26,753
So it was a very stern letter and Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) was very upset رضي الله عنه.

398
00:29:28,423 --> 00:29:30,334
When Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) reads the letter, he says:

399
00:29:30,358 --> 00:29:33,148
This is the work of the Left Handed man, meaning Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب),

400
00:29:33,529 --> 00:29:34,146
 who was left handed.

401
00:29:34,170 --> 00:29:38,637
 He said, this the work of the Left Handed man and he writes a letter. He says:

402
00:29:38,763 --> 00:29:45,714
أمَّا بَعد، فل امري ما تزوجت نساء حتى تمَّالِيَّ السُّرُور وكرت به دار

403
00:29:47,096 --> 00:29:51,254
I did not marry, until the victory was done.

404
00:29:51,883 --> 00:29:54,602
 Meaning we're celebrating victory, our victory is done

405
00:29:54,913 --> 00:29:59,800
and that's when I married I didn't marry while the fighting was raging and going on.

406
00:30:01,279 --> 00:30:07,174
وما تزوجت اِلَّا المرِاة لو عملت عليه من المدينة خاتمًا لم أبالي

407
00:30:08,197 --> 00:30:12,539
دعنِّي إستفرت خطبتي إليه من تحت قدمه

408
00:30:12,920 --> 00:30:16,936
He said: And I married the daughter of a man, whom if I was in Madina

409
00:30:17,487 --> 00:30:21,002
 it would be worth traveling all the way to marry his daughter.

410
00:30:22,196 --> 00:30:23,498
 But I was right there, next to him.

411
00:30:23,807 --> 00:30:26,999
 He was saying that Maja'ah(مجاعة) is a person among his people.

412
00:30:28,544 --> 00:30:33,396
He is a man, whom I would even travel from Madina all the way to him, to marry his daughter

413
00:30:34,002 --> 00:30:38,531
his character and his position, and Khalid(خالد) says:

414
00:30:39,388 --> 00:30:42,689
فإن كنت قد قحتلي ذالك لدين أو لدنيا أعتكتك

415
00:30:42,775 --> 00:30:47,684
If you had a justification, a religious or worldly justification for that

416
00:30:47,970 --> 00:30:50,210
 then you could be excused for blaming me for it.

417
00:30:50,438 --> 00:30:53,519
So, he is saying that, there is no reason to be angry with, what I did.

418
00:30:53,781 --> 00:30:54,686
And then he said;

419
00:30:55,315 --> 00:31:04,628
وأمَّا حسن عزائي عن قتل المسلمين فولله لو كان حزن يقي حياًّ أو يَرُدُّوْ مَيَّتًا لا أبقى حسن الحيَّ وَرَدِّ الْمَيِت

420
00:31:05,822 --> 00:31:09,392
In terms of my sadness for the dead Muslims.

421
00:31:09,989 --> 00:31:13,921
 If sadness would resurrect them from deaths

422
00:31:14,583 --> 00:31:17,352
then my sadness would be enough to bring them to life again.

423
00:31:18,520 --> 00:31:23,060
In other words, Khalid(خالد) is saying I am in pain for the ones that I lost from my army.

424
00:31:24,120 --> 00:31:25,969
I'm having a lot of sorrow for that.

425
00:31:26,302 --> 00:31:27,632
But what will sorrow do?

426
00:31:28,020 --> 00:31:33,450
 If sorrow would bring them back to life, I would have done that. And then he said;

427
00:31:33,688 --> 00:31:37,408
ولقد إقتحمت حتى أن يسم الحياء و ان قنت بالموت

428
00:31:38,224 --> 00:31:43,737
And I would throw myself among their ranks, until I would become certain

429
00:31:43,769 --> 00:31:45,700
that I would die and I would give up living.

430
00:31:46,322 --> 00:31:50,971
 Khalid(خالد) is saying that I have put myself in situations where I would lose hope in living

431
00:31:51,533 --> 00:31:55,113
and see death as a certainty meaning Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد)

432
00:31:56,744 --> 00:31:58,574
and this would respond to the orientalist

433
00:31:58,598 --> 00:32:00,812
who say Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) was looking after pleasure

434
00:32:01,451 --> 00:32:04,598
Khalid(خالد) was saying that I have sought after death.

435
00:32:04,866 --> 00:32:08,567
 I have thrown myself among them, to die.

436
00:32:09,082 --> 00:32:10,853
Nevertheless, I wouldn't get it.

437
00:32:11,337 --> 00:32:12,499
And At-Tabari(ألطبري) would say

438
00:32:13,012 --> 00:32:15,201
that when Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) would throw himself among the enemy

439
00:32:15,588 --> 00:32:16,941
ياكلو كل شيءٍ أمامة

440
00:32:16,980 --> 00:32:20,102
He would eat everything around him, everything around him would just fall down dead.

441
00:32:20,825 --> 00:32:23,159
 Khalid(خالد) was looking for death, but nobody could kill him.

442
00:32:24,266 --> 00:32:24,960
So Khalid(خالد) was saying;

443
00:32:24,985 --> 00:32:26,180
حتى أن قنت موت

444
00:32:27,075 --> 00:32:28,566
I'm not entangled to Duniyah(دُنِيَّا)

445
00:32:28,590 --> 00:32:31,838
there is no Tathaqul Ilad-Duniyah(تثاكل إلى الدنيا) with Khalid Ibn Walid رضي الله عنه.

446
00:32:32,139 --> 00:32:37,457
 In fact, let me mention this to you, Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) marrying twice and it might be interpreted otherwise.

447
00:32:38,049 --> 00:32:40,756
 Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد), this is his own statement. He said:

448
00:32:42,052 --> 00:32:46,641
 If a beautiful woman, whom I love is married to me

449
00:32:47,035 --> 00:32:55,294
or I am given the news of a newborn male child that is less dearer to my heart,

450
00:32:55,510 --> 00:33:03,228
then sleeping in a tent, in a cold windy night, planning to ambush my enemy the next day.

451
00:33:05,415 --> 00:33:07,896
Now I want the single brothers to think about that.

452
00:33:09,345 --> 00:33:12,277
 The ones, who want to get married you know how much you love marriage

453
00:33:12,301 --> 00:33:16,998
 you are so eager to get married. Khalid(خالد) is saying that

454
00:33:17,361 --> 00:33:21,694
me being married to a woman, whom I love is less dear to my heart

455
00:33:21,861 --> 00:33:25,623
than spending the night in a cold tent planning to attack my enemy.

456
00:33:26,892 --> 00:33:28,544
Do you understand what that means?

457
00:33:29,163 --> 00:33:30,552
The next day he could be dead.

458
00:33:31,574 --> 00:33:33,023
Plus he is a leader of an army

459
00:33:33,047 --> 00:33:36,724
and a leader of army bears the responsibility of any loss that happens.

460
00:33:37,501 --> 00:33:43,192
 I mean, you can't show your face to the Muslims after you lost, it's shame.

461
00:33:44,143 --> 00:33:48,327
Before a person is giving a speech or before a person is going to a very important deal.

462
00:33:48,450 --> 00:33:53,942
Their heart is pounding, they feel pain in their guts, butterflies in their stomach

463
00:33:53,966 --> 00:33:56,149
because of the presence of the situation.

464
00:33:57,051 --> 00:34:00,601
Can you think about Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) planning an attack for the next day?

465
00:34:02,325 --> 00:34:06,774
But that is more dear to him, than marriage.

466
00:34:07,954 --> 00:34:12,858
That's how much they love Jihad(جهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله), they love Shahadah(شَهَادَة).

467
00:34:14,425 --> 00:34:18,694
And then he said because Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) said that you were tricked by Maja'ah(مجاعة). He said:

468
00:34:19,348 --> 00:34:23,956
وأمَّا خَدَعت مجاعة إيَّائ أن راعي إني لم أختي رائي يومي

469
00:34:24,472 --> 00:34:28,072
ولم يكل لي علم با لغيب وقد صنع الله للمسلمين خيرًا

470
00:34:28,590 --> 00:34:30,681
And saying that Maja'ah(مجاعة) tricked me.

471
00:34:30,959 --> 00:34:36,818
My opinion was not wrong on that day and I do not know the unseen.

472
00:34:36,976 --> 00:34:43,352
Khalid(خالد) is saying I base my opinion according to what I can see and I don't know the unseen.

473
00:34:43,839 --> 00:34:46,013
وقد صنع الله للمسلمين خيرًا

474
00:34:46,244 --> 00:34:51,914
And Allah has done the Muslims good, they have won, and the end belongs to Al-Muttaqeen(ألمتقين).

475
00:34:53,255 --> 00:34:54,666
We have achieved victory, so.

476
00:34:55,194 --> 00:34:59,126
Yes, Maja'ah(مجاعة) did trick me, but his people became Muslim

477
00:34:59,585 --> 00:35:02,410
because Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) it is mentioned At-Tabari(ألطبري) that

478
00:35:02,434 --> 00:35:04,868
 he sent a letter to Khalid(خالد), telling him:

479
00:35:05,090 --> 00:35:09,717
Whoever lands in your hand from the people of Abu Hanifa(أبوحنيفه), execute them.

480
00:35:10,971 --> 00:35:16,877
But he received this letter after he already executed the truce between him and Maja'ah(مجاعة).

481
00:35:17,131 --> 00:35:20,958
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) wanted to punish the Murtaddeen(مرتدين) severely.

482
00:35:21,723 --> 00:35:24,881
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ, His Qadar(قَدَر) is that Maja'ah(مجاعة) and his people became Muslim.

483
00:35:26,189 --> 00:35:28,834
When Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) received the letter, that soften his heart a bit.

484
00:35:29,698 --> 00:35:31,560
But then there are some people from Quraish(قُرَيْشْ)

485
00:35:31,584 --> 00:35:36,261
and also Abu Barzal-Aslami(أبوبرزلأسلمي), who came to argue on behalf of Khalid(خالد).

486
00:35:37,425 --> 00:35:41,429
He said, Abu Barzal-Aslami(أبوبرزلأسلمي), he said: O Khalifah(خليفه) of the Messenger of Allah,

487
00:35:42,124 --> 00:35:46,748
Khalid(خالد) cannot be characterized as having of lacking courage

488
00:35:47,283 --> 00:35:50,233
or of betraying his trust to the Muslims.

489
00:35:50,915 --> 00:35:59,700
Khalid(خالد) has searched has put himself in situations in search of martyrdom, and he did his best but he won.

490
00:36:01,334 --> 00:36:06,772
And the truce that he concluded with the people was a pleasing truce to him.

491
00:36:07,362 --> 00:36:09,908
And you cannot say that his view was wrong

492
00:36:09,935 --> 00:36:17,349
because he saw women covering the roofs, and he thought that they were men.

493
00:36:17,650 --> 00:36:20,879
Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) said: I believe what you say

494
00:36:21,291 --> 00:36:24,924
 and you have given me a more valid excuse for Khalid(خالد) than his letter.

495
00:36:25,336 --> 00:36:29,353
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) saw that this is more of an excuse for Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد)

496
00:36:29,623 --> 00:36:31,450
and the issue was over with

497
00:36:31,803 --> 00:36:37,985
and Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه forgave, Khalid Ibn Walid رضي الله عنه ورضي الله عنهم أجمعين.

498
00:36:38,837 --> 00:36:41,476
 Last thing regarding the Yamamah(يمامة).

499
00:36:42,127 --> 00:36:43,714
When the news reached the Muslims

500
00:36:44,171 --> 00:36:46,890
وإستحر قتل في حافظة القرآن

501
00:36:47,649 --> 00:36:52,004
There are so many Huffaaz(حفاظ) of Qur'an killed.

502
00:36:53,156 --> 00:36:55,858
 Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه went to Abu Bakr(ابوبكر)

503
00:36:56,493 --> 00:36:58,447
it show you how drastic that event was?

504
00:36:58,582 --> 00:36:59,915
He went to Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) and said,

505
00:37:00,557 --> 00:37:04,714
There were so many of the Sahabah(صحابه) the memorize of Qur'an who were killed

506
00:37:05,678 --> 00:37:13,013
and Qur'an is in the hearts of men and if the men go, then Qur'an might be lost.

507
00:37:14,303 --> 00:37:17,213
So why don't you compile Qur'an?

508
00:37:18,456 --> 00:37:24,051
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) said: How can you ask me to do something that Rasool Allah ﷺ did not do?

509
00:37:24,794 --> 00:37:26,576
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) argued with him.

510
00:37:27,238 --> 00:37:30,488
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه thought over it

511
00:37:31,678 --> 00:37:35,172
and he came to adopt the opinion of Umar(عُمَر).

512
00:37:36,883 --> 00:37:48,703
So, Zaid Bin Thabit Al-Ansaari(زيد بن ثابت ألأنصاري) a 21 year old young man from Al-Ansaar(اَلْاَنْصَار) received a message saying that the Khalifah(خليفه) wants to meet you.

513
00:37:49,583 --> 00:37:51,922
He's narrating that he said: I go to meet the Khalifah(خليفه)

514
00:37:52,433 --> 00:37:56,086
and I find Umar(عُمَر) sitting next to him. And then the Khalifah(خليفه) tells me:

515
00:37:56,551 --> 00:38:00,520
Umar(عُمَر) came to me and told me that there are many Huffaz(حفاظ) of Qur'an, who were killed.

516
00:38:00,968 --> 00:38:03,491
So why don't you compile Qur'an to protect it?

517
00:38:03,964 --> 00:38:06,327
So I told them: This is something that Rasool Ullah did not do.

518
00:38:06,987 --> 00:38:11,426
But then I thought about it, and came to agree with Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب).

519
00:38:11,759 --> 00:38:17,410
So now I am giving you the responsibility of compiling Al-Qur'an.

520
00:38:19,186 --> 00:38:25,071
Zaid Bin Thabit(زيد بن ثابت) said: If Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) would load on top of my shoulders, a mountain

521
00:38:25,635 --> 00:38:29,441
 it would be lighter in weight than the mission he gave to me.

522
00:38:31,750 --> 00:38:38,953
 But Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) said: The reason why I'm appointing you to do that he said;

523
00:38:40,601 --> 00:38:47,860
وانك رجل شاب عاقل لا نتحمك وقد كنت تكتب الوحي ألي رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم

524
00:38:48,442 --> 00:38:54,893
You are a young man, you are mature and wise, and we trust you for this mission

525
00:38:55,469 --> 00:38:59,136
 and you used to write the revelation for Rasool Allah ﷺ.

526
00:38:59,874 --> 00:39:05,521
And Zaid Bin Thabit(زيد بن ثابت) was one of the scholars of Qur'an even though he was at that young age.

527
00:39:06,023 --> 00:39:06,461
 So he said;

528
00:39:06,485 --> 00:39:10,449
I had to go around collecting Qur'an from the hearts of men

529
00:39:10,900 --> 00:39:13,897
and collecting all of the manuscripts of Qur'an that existed.

530
00:39:14,383 --> 00:39:16,270
He picked up Usub(عصب)

531
00:39:16,525 --> 00:39:19,960
 Usub(عصب) is palm leaves, they use to write on palm leaves

532
00:39:20,285 --> 00:39:27,303
and they use to write on flat, carved rock and they use write on the shoulder bone of camels.

533
00:39:27,440 --> 00:39:32,240
The shoulder bone is a flat plate, so they would write on that plate.

534
00:39:33,308 --> 00:39:34,928
And they would also write on leather.

535
00:39:35,095 --> 00:39:40,121
So he said: I had to gather all of those pieces and then I compiled the Qur'an.

536
00:39:40,261 --> 00:39:45,305
And the Mus'haf(مصحف), the original copy was with Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق), until he passed away.

537
00:39:45,801 --> 00:39:47,570
It was handed down to Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب).

538
00:39:47,831 --> 00:39:51,428
And when Umar(عُمَر) passed away it was given to Hafsa(حفصه),

539
00:39:51,674 --> 00:39:54,714
 the daughter of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه, Umm-Ul-Mo'mineen(أم المؤمنين).

540
00:39:55,546 --> 00:40:00,577
So that was the story of the beginning of the compiling of Qur'an.

541
00:40:00,960 --> 00:40:03,412
صَلَّى الله عَلى سَيَّدِنَا محمد وَعَلى اَلِهِ وَ صَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ

